WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.956
Detection tuning is not failure.

2
00:00:01.956 --> 00:00:03.443
It is part of the lifecycle.

3
00:00:03.443 --> 00:00:07.813
Real environments reveal patterns that are hard to predict during initial design.

4
00:00:07.813 --> 00:00:14.588
Analysts may discover repeated false positives, missing context, unclear severity, or workflow problems.

5
00:00:14.588 --> 00:00:17.811
That feedback helps detection engineers improve the signal.

6
00:00:17.811 --> 00:00:26.062
Tuning may refine conditions, add exclusions, improve enrichment, update documentation, change severity, or adjust routing.

7
00:00:26.062 --> 00:00:29.435
The goal is better usefulness, not just fewer alerts.

8
00:00:29.435 --> 00:00:33.915
A healthy program treats feedback as a source of improvement rather than criticism.

9
00:00:33.915 --> 00:00:37.976
The detection gets stronger when engineers and analysts learn from each other.
